  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1221 AM CDT Tue Sep 15 2026\n\nThe upper level ridge over the southeastern U.S. will expand\nwestward into our area from Wednesday through Saturday. The ridge\nwill not be quite as strong as it has been the last week, but \ntemperatures will still be well above normal- in the mid 90s to \nnear 100 degrees. As mentioned in the previous AFD a pattern shift\nlate in the weekend into early next week. An upper level trough is\nforecast to deepen over the Rockies which will help to weaken the\nupper ridge and send a frontal boundary into our area. There\nremains uncertainty in how the large scale pattern will evolve\nearly next week so will stick with the model blends for this\nforecast package. By Monday highs are forecast to be closer to\nseasonal normals (upper 80s to lower 90s) with a 30-50% chance of\nscattered showers on both Sunday and Monday.",
